        "edits": [
          "  }, [serverSnapshotIsUsed, getSnapshot, subscribe]);"
        ],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues with one change in `index.ts`. The effect's dependency list was empty (`[]`), and it is now `[serverSnapshotIsUsed, getSnapshot, subscribe]` (line 78). That covers every value the two rules said was missing. I couldn't re-run oxlint because the command needed approval, so this hasn't been confirmed by a fresh lint run.\n\nWhat changes at runtime:\n- **`serverSnapshotIsUsed`** never changes (its setter is thrown away), so listing it does nothing.\n- **Stable `subscribe` / `getSnapshot`** (defined outside the component or memoized): no change. The effect still runs once on mount.\n- **Inline `subscribe` / `getSnapshot`**: the hook now unsubscribes and subscribes again whenever their identity changes, which can be every render. This matches React's own `useSyncExternalStore`, which the stub says hono/jsx follows. It also fixes a real bug: before, the store callback kept using the first render's `getSnapshot`. If that function depended on props (say `() => store.get(id)`), it kept reading the old value after `id` changed.\n\nThe other option was to store the first-render functions in refs. That would keep the original subscribe-once behavior exactly, but it also keeps the stale `getSnapshot` bug. I chose to list the dependencies because the rule's help text recommends it.",
